# UI / UX (mobile-led)

**Authority for interaction & visual UX.** Layout breakpoints → `18-mobile-first-responsive.mdc`. A11y shells → `05-components.mdc`. CWV → `09` / `10`. Preserve brand (`dq-*` gold/navy) — no alternate theme.

## Hierarchy & composition

- **One job per section:** one headline + short support; avoid stuffing stats, schedules, and promo chips into the same block
- **First viewport (marketing):** brand/H1, one short lead, one CTA group, optional hero media — no card grids or secondary marketing in the hero
- Prefer existing shells (`PageHeroHeader`, `LeafHero`, `SectionHeaderRow`, `CenteredSectionHeader`, `ContentCard`) before new chrome
- Cards only when they wrap a **single** primary action (`ContentCard`) — no nested competing links
- Clear visual order: H1 → sections → supporting lists; do not rely on color alone for meaning

## Touch & targets

- Controls ≥ **44×44px** (`TW_TOUCH` / `min-h-11` / `min-w-11` for icon buttons)
- Keep ≥8px gap between adjacent tap targets
- Primary CTA within easy thumb reach on long pages (section CTA or leaf banner — not only footer)
- Floating/sticky UI (WhatsApp, sticky header) must **not** cover form fields, focus rings, or leaf CTAs
- Mobile nav: focus trap correct; close control ≥44px; `env(safe-area-inset-top/bottom)` respected

## Forms & feedback

- Full-width fields on mobile (`TW_FORM_*`); stack with `TW_GRID_2` (1 → `sm:2`)
- Correct `type` + `inputMode` (`tel`, `email`); visible labels; errors beside the field
- Status: `aria-busy` / `aria-live` for submit; disable double-submit
- Turnstile / heavy widgets: load on intersect — never block first paint

## Motion & feedback

- Respect `prefers-reduced-motion` + `motion-reduce:hover:translate-y-0`
- Prefer opacity/transform; avoid animating layout that causes CLS on mobile
- Reveal: CSS-visible on mobile / no-JS (`09`); do not gate content behind JS
- `:focus-visible` rings always visible — never `outline-none` alone
- Active press: `active:translate-y-0` / brightness — confirm taps without hover-only states

## Density & readability

- Comfortable section padding (`TW_SECTION_PY`); do not pack multi-column tables on phones — stack or scroll with clear affordance
- Long Urdu lines: prefer narrower prose containers on mobile; keep leading ≥1.9 (`03-rtl-urdu.mdc`)
- Empty/error states: Urdu copy + clear next action (`app/error.tsx` pattern)

## Anti-patterns

- Desktop-only hover as the sole affordance
- Pill/chip clusters and multi-CTA rows that wrap into unreadable stacks
- Inset “floating” hero cards that fight the full-bleed leaf/home heroes
- Inventing a second design language (purple gradients, cream/serif defaults, dark mode)

